The RaceDay API is a RESTful Web API built with ASP.NET Core and raw ADO.NET (`SqlConnection`) for managing sports events, enrollments, and results,
featuring strict Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) managed via JWT authentication. The system serves two primary roles: **Organisers**, who can create and manage events, 
define categories and fees, view all event enrollments, and post final race results; and **Participants**, who can view events, enroll in categories
to generate a race number, and view their own enrollment history and personal results. To set up the project, you must execute the provided SQL script in SQL Server Management
Studio to create the `RaceDay` database, update the `DefaultConnection`
string in `appsettings.json` to point to your local SQL instance, and ensure the JWT configuration keys are populated. Once configured, restore dependencies with `dotnet restore
` and run the application using `dotnet run` to access the Swagger UI for endpoint testing.To run the unit tests locally, ensure a separate `RaceDay_Test` database is configured within 
`CustomWebApplicationFactory.cs` and execute `dotnet test`. Additionally, the repository includes a GitHub Actions CI workflow (`.github/workflows/dotnet.yml`) that automatically builds the solution
and runs all tests upon every push to the main branch.Security is prioritized through BCrypt password hashing, JWT token validation, strict role-based endpoint authorization, and database-level ownership
checks ensuring Organisers can only modify their own events.
